{"seconds": 72.3, "exit": 0, "final": "After Kh7, White has Qxc5 winning the queen! So the position is completely winning for White.\n\nSo the main line is:\n1. **Bxg7+!** Kxg7 (best; Kh7 allows similar lines)\n2. **Qf7+** Kh8 (forced)\n3. **Qxf8+** and White has won decisively (rook and leads to mate or total domination)\n\nThe best move is **Bxg7+** - a deflection/removal of the defender (the g7 pawn that helps protect the king) combined with a discovered attack from the bishop.\n\n**Summary for the coaching note:**\nThe key is that Black's king on h8 is trapped in the corner with g7 as the only escape pawn. By removing that pawn with check using the bishop, White exposes the king to a mating attack. The queen can then deliver checks on f7 and f8, leading to checkmate or catastrophic material loss. The pattern: **look for trapped kings, especially those with limited escape squares** - removing their defenders with forcing moves often leads to tactics.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bxg7+\", \"line\": [\"Bxg7+\", \"Kxg7\", \"Qf7+\", \"Kh8\", \"Qxf8#\"], \"motifs\": [\"discoveredAttack\", \"attraction\", \"backRankMate\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50", "move": "Qxf8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50", "move": "Qe8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50", "move": "Bxf8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50", "move": "Qf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/6p1/p3Q2p/P1q1B3/7P/6P1/5P2/6K1 w - - 7 50", "move":